# Localization

Workit serves English (`en`, default) and Albanian (`sq`). The request language is
resolved from the `Accept-Language` header by `UseRequestLocalization` in
`Program.cs`, which sets `CultureInfo.CurrentUICulture`.

## Translation catalog

- Strings live in `Workit.Core/Shared/Localization/Resources/translations.{en,sq}.json`
  as a flat `key: value` map, embedded in `Workit.Core` (`<WithCulture>false</WithCulture>`
  so `.sq.` is not treated as a satellite culture).
- `ILocalizer` (singleton `JsonLocalizer`) resolves keys against the current culture,
  then English, then returns the key unchanged. Inject it where translation is needed.
- `Language.Supported` / `Language.Resolve` are the single source of truth for
  supported codes. Add a language by extending both and adding a resource file.

## Rules

- User-facing message text goes through `ILocalizer`, keyed, never hard-coded inline.
- `DomainException` / `NotFoundException` take a **catalog key** as their message
  (`throw new NotFoundException("error.jobOpeningNotFound")`). `ApiExceptionWriter`
  translates it. A plain sentence still works (it is returned verbatim when absent
  from the catalog) but new code uses keys under `error.*`.
- FluentValidation: built-in messages resolve via `WorkitValidatorLanguageManager`
  (keys `validation.<ValidatorName>`); property names via the global
  `DisplayNameResolver` (keys `property.<PropertyName>`). Custom messages use
  `.WithMessage(_ => localizer.Translate("validation.<feature>.<rule>"))`, not a
  literal string.
- Enums exposed in responses get a sibling localized label
  (`localizer.Enum(value)`, keys `enum.<EnumType>.<Value>`); the raw enum value is
  still returned. Shape job-opening responses through `JobOpeningPresentation`.
- User-generated job-opening text is translated by the submitting business, stored
  in the `job_openings.Translations` jsonb column keyed by language, with
  `ContentLanguage` naming the base language. `JobOpening.ResolveContent(language)`
  does field-by-field fallback to the base values. Do not machine-translate.
